* DC input: a live supply is plugged in. Cable - fuse F102 - D105 - C117 - L103 - C112, C113, TVS D106.
* The supply has no resistance of its own. The ceramic capacitors lose capacitance with voltage:
* C(V) = C0 / (1 + (V/V0)^2), fitted to the maker's curve of the 2.2 uF / 100 V X7R part
* (2.2, 2.0, 1.53, 1.02 uF at 5, 12, 24, 40 V). The TVS is at the upper end of its breakdown range
* (31.9 V; 42.1 V at 14.3 A). The converter is still off: it only starts after its soft start.
.param vsup=24
.param lcab=3.45u
.param rcab=0.119
.param rfuse=0.05
.param c0=2.2u
.param v0=36.26
.param vbr=31.9
.param rtvs=0.713
V1 src 0 PWL(0 0 20n {vsup})
Lcab src n1 {lcab}
Rcab n1 n2 {rcab + rfuse}
D105 n2 vdcr SS34
.model SS34 D(IS=5u RS=0.04 N=1.1 CJO=300p M=0.4 BV=45 IBV=1m)
R117 vdcr c117 5m
Xc117 c117 0 mlcc k=1
L103 vdcr l103 2.2u
R103 l103 vdc 0.10
R112 vdc c112 2.5m
Xc112 c112 0 mlcc k=2
Vtvs vdc tvs 0
Btvs tvs 0 I = v(tvs) > {vbr} ? (v(tvs) - {vbr}) / {rtvs} : 0
Rload vdc 0 100k
* k capacitors in parallel. The charge Q(V) = C0 V0 atan(V/V0) is formed as a voltage (1 V per uC) and
* differentiated by a 1 uF capacitor; that current is mirrored into the terminals.
.subckt mlcc p n k=1
Bq q 0 V = 1e6 * {k*c0*v0} * atan(v(p,n)/{v0})
Vs q qc 0
Cq qc 0 1u
Fc p n Vs 1
Rp p n 1g
.ends
.option method=gear reltol=1e-4
.tran 5n 400u uic
.control
set noaskquit
run
meas tran v_converter max v(vdc)
meas tran v_c117 max v(vdcr)
meas tran i_tvs max i(vtvs)
quit
.endc
.end
